I've left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read`, so it has no filesystem or HTTP authority to write the log or call the metadata service. Adding those imports would widen the node's authority beyond what it was granted. Operations would need to route those through a node that holds the right capabilities.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

/// Key within the `subscriptions` store that holds the newline-separated URL list.
const STATE_KEY: &str = "urls";

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get(STATE_KEY) {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

